Donald Trump promised Americans a "Golden Age" when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1815b358-d7c9-11f1-ad2c-2b007ce09517</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:56:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? It's Election Day in the United States, with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of midterm results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump's second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all? 
